---

## 0. MISSION

Evolve ATM from a single sequential money-search loop into a bounded, evidence-driven SWARM that increases the probability and speed of reaching real withdrawable money.

The swarm is NOT a group chat of agents and NOT an excuse to multiply model calls.

The design principle is:

> parallel perception + independent falsification + dynamic resource allocation + stigmergic shared state; deterministic authority remains centralized.

ATM's economic identity remains unchanged:

- Month-1 target: `REALIZED_WITHDRAWABLE_USD >= 500`;
- target rises every month according to the growth law established by ORDER-002;
- optimize money velocity, not headline bounty size;
- short-duration, live, claimable, objectively checkable work dominates long-horizon speculative work;
- only externally verified released/withdrawable value is money.

---

## 1. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANT

Exactly ONE deterministic ATM supervisor remains authoritative.

The swarm may propose, observe, falsify, rank, work, check and monitor.

The swarm MUST NOT independently author economic truth, mutate the validated payment ledger, bypass claim/submission adapters, create duplicate claims, launch a second supervisor, or directly sign/spend/transfer funds.

Canonical separation:

```text
SWARM = perception + discovery + falsification + bounded work + monitoring
SUPERVISOR = lifecycle authority + scheduling + leases + policy
PAYMENT ADAPTERS = authoritative external settlement verification
LEDGER = single-writer economic truth
```

No model writes `REALIZED_WITHDRAWABLE_USD` or equivalent monetary truth.

---

## 2. WHY SWARM EXISTS

The bottleneck in ATM is not merely model intelligence. It is coverage and reaction time across many changing external opportunity surfaces.

A sequential agent can be waiting on one HTTP request, one payer, one marketplace, one review or one task while money appears elsewhere.

The swarm exists to reduce:

- time-to-discovery;
- time-to-falsification;
- time-to-claim;
- idle time while external tasks await review/payment;
- dependence on one model/provider/search strategy;
- opportunity loss caused by stale information.

The swarm MUST earn its complexity. If measured money-velocity proxy or live progression does not improve relative to the sequential baseline, reduce concurrency or revert to sequential scheduling without losing state.

---

## 3. STIGMERGIC COORDINATION — NO AGENT CHATROOM

Agents coordinate through a local durable shared Money Board, not free-form conversations.

Preferred implementation: local SQLite with WAL mode or another equally durable transactional local store. Do NOT use GitHub comments as the high-frequency internal swarm datastore. GitHub remains the human/ARQ command bus from ORDER-002.

Each normalized opportunity record must include when obtainable:

- canonical opportunity ID;
- rail/source;
- authoritative URL/API identity;
- task archetype;
- created/updated timestamps;
- last authoritative verification time;
- payer/buyer/maintainer activity evidence;
- funding evidence;
- net reward estimate;
- fees;
- claim mechanics;
- claimability status;
- competition/attempt/submission count;
- estimated agent work minutes;
- acceptance predicate/mechanism;
- review latency estimate;
- settlement latency estimate;
- payout rail;
- payout eligibility constraints;
- evidence confidence;
- current ATM money-velocity score;
- score components;
- status/lease owner;
- rejection/falsification reasons;
- TTL/expiry;
- next revalidation time.

Agents write structured evidence and decisions. Do not copy large chain-of-thought text into shared state.

---

## 4. PHEROMONE / DECAY MODEL

Implement swarm-like signal reinforcement without magical language.

An opportunity receives a bounded `SWARM_SIGNAL` derived from the same economic factors as ORDER-002.

It MUST decay when evidence becomes old.

At minimum:

```text
SWARM_SIGNAL(t) = BASE_ECONOMIC_SCORE × FRESHNESS_DECAY × EVIDENCE_CONFIDENCE
```

Fresh authoritative evidence may reinforce the signal.

Negative evidence must sharply reduce it:

- payer inactive;
- task closed;
- reward unfunded;
- competitor/PR count jumps;
- claim lost;
- acceptance rules become ambiguous;
- payout method becomes unavailable;
- settlement latency increases materially.

Do not let old high-reward listings retain priority just because they once scored well.

---

## 5. SWARM POPULATION

Implement roles as bounded worker types under the single supervisor. Roles are logical capabilities, not necessarily permanent OS processes.

### SCOUTS

Run independent discovery strategies in parallel when capacity allows.

Initial scout specializations:

1. `SCOUT_AGENT_NATIVE` — WorkProtocol, Taskmarket, AgentPact/equivalent live API rails;
2. `SCOUT_OSS` — GitHub/Opire/Algora/project-native paid issues reconciled against upstream;
3. `SCOUT_MACHINE_JUDGED` — structured data, QA, eval, benchmark, validator-driven paid work;
4. `SCOUT_LONG_TAIL` — discover previously unknown legitimate rails/payment predicates instead of repeatedly searching the same named marketplaces.

A scout outputs only normalized candidates + evidence. It has no claim authority.

### FALSIFIERS

At least one independent fresh session attempts to kill high-scoring candidates before scarce WORK capacity is committed.

Falsification checks include:

- stale listing;
- upstream mismatch;
- funding absent;
- buyer/payer dead;
- payout inaccessible;
- AI/automation prohibited;
- task already solved;
- duplicate/open PR saturation;
- hidden onboarding/KYC/stake/capital cost;
- deadline impossible;
- acceptance subjective or unverifiable;
- expected settlement too slow;
- task complexity materially underestimated.

Falsifiers produce structured verdict/evidence, never economic truth.

### CLAIM ADAPTER

Claiming remains deterministic and idempotent under supervisor authority.

Exactly one lease holder may attempt a claim for a canonical opportunity.

### WORKER

Start with exactly ONE concurrent active WORK slot.

Only increase to two after ARQ proves:

- workspace isolation;
- state isolation;
- provider/rate-limit headroom;
- no substantial degradation of task completion time;
- no duplicate GitHub/rail side effects;
- Windows host remains healthy.

Do not equate more workers with better swarm performance.

### CHECKER

Fresh independent one-shot session, separate context from worker where possible.

It re-fetches acceptance criteria and evaluates actual artifact/diff/tests.

### WATCHERS

Cheap asynchronous watchers monitor claimed/submitted/review/payment states while scouts continue working.

Watchers must use APIs/conditional requests and backoff whenever available. Never waste model calls merely polling deterministic status.

### PAYMENT WATCHER

Deterministic adapter only. No LLM payment inference.

---

## 6. DYNAMIC RESOURCE ALLOCATION / ECONOMIC AUCTION

Do not statically give every role equal compute.

Each candidate competes for scarce execution capacity using a supervisor-computed score.

Base it on ORDER-002's money velocity and add evidence confidence + marginal value of allocating another worker.

Conceptually:

```text
RESOURCE_BID(task) =
ATM_MONEY_VELOCITY(task)
× EVIDENCE_CONFIDENCE
× MARGINAL_VALUE_OF_COMPUTE
```

Do not fake precision. Use evidence-derived/calibrated heuristics and update them from outcomes.

Examples:

- a $20 task claimable now, 10-minute fix, live payer, zero competitors can outrank a $500 bounty with 10 PRs;
- a submitted task waiting for review gets a cheap watcher, not a full worker;
- a high-score candidate that fails falsification immediately releases its resources;
- if one rail repeatedly produces stale inventory, scouts spend less capacity there until new evidence revives it.

---

## 7. LEASES / DUPLICATE PREVENTION

Swarm concurrency MUST NOT create duplicate economic actions.

Implement transactional leases keyed by canonical opportunity/action identity.

Required lease classes include:

- VERIFY lease;
- CLAIM lease;
- WORK lease;
- SUBMIT lease.

Leases have owner, acquired timestamp, expiry, heartbeat/renewal when appropriate and terminal release state.

After crash/restart, stale leases must be safely recoverable from authoritative external state.

Two agents racing for the same task must collapse into one authorized economic action.

Idempotency keys from existing adapters remain authoritative.

---

## 8. PROVIDER / MODEL DIVERSITY

Swarm intelligence SHOULD exploit heterogeneous search/reasoning when available, but models are replaceable workers, not authorities.

Allow different configured models/providers for scout/falsifier/worker/checker roles when economically justified.

The system must survive one provider being quota-limited/down by reducing or rerouting capacity rather than stopping the whole swarm.

Provider choice itself may be scored by:

- observed success rate by role;
- latency;
- rate-limit history;
- cost if non-zero costs are ever explicitly permitted;
- structured-output reliability;
- coding/test performance.

For current zero-capital operation, do not silently introduce paid model/API usage.

Do not spawn model sessions solely for artificial diversity. Diversity must have measurable informational/execution value.

---

## 9. RESOURCE GOVERNOR

Implement hard local budgets so swarm behavior cannot thrash the OWNER machine or provider quotas.

Configurable caps at minimum:

- max concurrent scout sessions;
- max concurrent falsifier sessions;
- max active WORK slots;
- max total model subprocesses;
- per-provider concurrency;
- per-provider failure/429 circuit breaker;
- task timeout;
- CPU/memory pressure thresholds if reliably measurable;
- network backoff;
- max queued candidates;
- max evidence age before mandatory revalidation.

Start conservatively. Increase concurrency only from measured headroom.

On resource pressure, shed capacity in this order:

1. low-score speculative scouts;
2. duplicate/low-information falsifiers;
3. low-priority watchers by increasing polling interval;

Preserve in-flight claimed WORK, payment verification and supervisor/control-plane health.

---

## 10. SWARM STATE MACHINE

Opportunities move through explicit deterministic states, e.g.:

```text
DISCOVERED
→ NORMALIZED
→ VERIFYING
→ VERIFIED
→ FALSIFYING
→ ELIGIBLE
→ CLAIM_LEASED
→ CLAIMED
→ WORK_LEASED
→ WORKING
→ CHECKING
→ SUBMIT_LEASED
→ SUBMITTED
→ MONITORING
→ ACCEPTED/REJECTED
→ PAYMENT_VERIFY
→ PAID
```

Rejected/stale/lost opportunities retain reasons/evidence for calibration but do not remain in active queues.

Transitions remain supervisor-controlled.

